      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
